From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: babarot <b4b4r07@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:26:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Hide review requests that no longer need a review

A review request stayed listed after someone else merged, closed or
approved the pull request, and gh-news filters cannot see a pull
request's state. hide_resolved_review_requests lists the states that
hide one ("merged", "closed", "approved"). While it is set, open review
requests are checked on every refresh, batched into one GraphQL query
per 50 pull requests: a REST and a GraphQL call each went over GitHub's
hourly limit with a few dozen of them. Empty, the default, fetches
nothing.
